    "gold_solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"VRPTW\")\n    m.setParam('TimeLimit', 300)\n\n    # --- Data ---\n    n_customers = 5\n    n_vehicles = 3\n    Q = 36  # vehicle capacity\n    vehicle_fixed_cost = 100.0\n    depot = [50, 50]\n    customers = [[92, 41], [39, 17], [74, 33], [82, 78], [91, 57]]\n    demands = [18, 16, 10, 18, 5]\n    time_windows = [[0, 299], [67, 120], [35, 128], [37, 128], [49, 144], [58, 110]]\n    service_times = [9, 13, 10, 9, 5]\n\n    # Node 0 = depot, nodes 1..N = customers\n    N = n_customers\n    nodes = list(range(N + 1))\n    cust_nodes = list(range(1, N + 1))\n\n    # Coordinates: index 0 = depot, 1..N = customers\n    coords = [depot] + customers\n\n    # COMPUTE distance matrix from coordinates\n    dist = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                dist[(i,j)] = math.sqrt(\n                    (coords[i][0]-coords[j][0])**2 +\n                    (coords[i][1]-coords[j][1])**2)\n\n    # Service time by node (depot = 0)\n    svc = [0] + service_times\n\n    # Big-M for time linking\n    T_max = time_windows[0][1]\n    max_svc = max(service_times)\n    max_dist = max(dist.values())\n    M = T_max + max_svc + max_dist + 1\n\n    # --- Variables ---\n    # Arc variables (binary)\n    x = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                x[(i,j)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Arc_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # Load variables (MTZ subtour elimination)\n    u = {}\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        u[i] = m.addVar(lb=demands[i-1], ub=Q, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Load_{i}\")\n\n    # Time variables\n    t = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        a, b = time_windows[i]\n        t[i] = m.addVar(lb=a, ub=b, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Time_{i}\")\n    # Fix depot departure to time 0\n    t[0].ub = 0.0\n\n    # --- Objective ---\n    # Minimize travel distance + vehicle fixed costs\n    obj = quicksum(dist[(i,j)] * x[(i,j)] for i in nodes for j in nodes if i != j)\n    obj += quicksum(vehicle_fixed_cost * x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes)\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # --- Constraints ---\n    # 1. Each customer has exactly one outgoing arc\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for j in nodes if j != i) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitOut_C{i}\")\n\n    # 2. Each customer has exactly one incoming arc\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for i in nodes if i != j) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitIn_C{j}\")\n\n    # 3. At most K vehicles leave the depot\n    m.addConstr(\n        quicksum(x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes) <= n_vehicles,\n        name=\"VehicleLimit\")\n\n    # 4. MTZ subtour elimination\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        for j in cust_nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    u[i] - u[j] + Q * x[(i,j)] <= Q - demands[j-1],\n                    name=f\"MTZ_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # 5. Time linking: if arc (i,j) is used, arrival at j >= departure from i\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        for i in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    t[i] - t[j] + M * x[(i,j)] <= M - svc[i] - dist[(i,j)],\n                    name=f\"TimeLink_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Subject: Routing and Scheduling Requirements for Time-Windowed Deliveries\n\nTeam,\n\nWe are planning a delivery run from our central depot using a fleet of identical vehicles. All vehicles will depart the depot at time 0 and each must complete a single, continuous trip that returns to the depot before it closes. Our task is to determine which customers each vehicle should serve, in what sequence, and at what times, so that every customer is visited exactly once and all operational requirements are met.\n\nChallenge overview:\n- Each vehicle leaves the depot at time 0, visits a sequence of customers, and returns to the depot before the end of the planning horizon.\n- Every customer must be served by exactly one vehicle. No split deliveries are allowed.\n- Travel time between any two locations is the straight-line distance between their coordinates, with an implicit speed of 1 unit of distance per unit of time.\n\nTime and service requirements:\n- Each customer has a specific delivery time window. Service must start within this window.\n- If a vehicle arrives before the window opens, it must wait on site until the earliest allowed time.\n- Each customer requires a defined service/unloading time. The vehicle departs a location at its arrival time plus the service time; if it arrives early and waits, departure occurs at the window open time plus the service time.\n\nCapacity and feasibility:\n- Vehicles have limited carrying capacity. The total demand assigned to a vehicle\u2019s route must not exceed its capacity at any point in the trip.\n- Each vehicle performs only one trip during the planning horizon: from the depot, through its assigned customers, and back to the depot.\n\nCost structure and planning objective:\n- Using a vehicle incurs a fixed deployment cost in addition to the cost associated with the distance traveled on its route.\n- Our goal is to produce a feasible set of routes that visit all customers exactly once, respect all time windows, service times, vehicle capacity limits, and the depot\u2019s return requirement, while minimizing total travel distance plus fixed deployment costs.\n- In practical terms, we will balance the trade-off between deploying more vehicles to shorten routes and using fewer vehicles with longer routes, always ensuring that all constraints are observed.\n\nDeliverables:\n- A detailed routing plan showing, for each deployed vehicle: the sequence of customer visits, planned arrival and departure times at each stop (including any waiting), and the expected return time to the depot before closing.\n- A summary of total distance traveled and the number of vehicles deployed, reflecting the combined travel and deployment costs.\n\nANNEX \u2013 Operations Data\n- Depot location: (50, 50)\n- Depot closing time: 299\n- Customer locations: Customer Locations (coordinates):\n  - C1: (92, 41)\n  - C2: (39, 17)\n  - C3: (74, 33)\n  - C4: (82, 78)\n  - C5: (91, 57)\n- Customer demands: Customer Demands:\n  - C1: 18 units\n  - C2: 16 units\n  - C3: 10 units\n  - C4: 18 units\n  - C5: 5 units\n- Customer time windows: Customer Time Windows [earliest, latest]:\n  - C1: [67, 120]\n  - C2: [35, 128]\n  - C3: [37, 128]\n  - C4: [49, 144]\n  - C5: [58, 110]\n- Service times: Service Times (minutes at customer):\n  - C1: 9\n  - C2: 13\n  - C3: 10\n  - C4: 9\n  - C5: 5\n- Vehicle capacity: 36\n- Number of vehicles available: 3\n- Fixed cost per vehicle deployed: 100.0",
